## Vercel Speed Insights Installation Report

### Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the Next.js portfolio project following the official Vercel documentation.

### Changes Made

#### 1. Package Installation
- **Added**: `@vercel/speed-insights` version 2.0.0 to project dependencies
- **Method**: Installed using `npm i @vercel/speed-insights`
- **Updated files**: 
  - `package.json` - Added dependency
  - `package-lock.json` - Updated lock file with new package and its dependencies

#### 2. Component Configuration
- **Modified**: `app/layout.tsx` (Root layout file)
- **Changes**:
  - Added import: `import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/next";`
  - Added `<SpeedInsights />` component inside the `<body>` tag after children
  - Reformatted body element to multiline for better readability

### Implementation Details

Following the official Vercel Speed Insights quickstart guide (https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart), I:

1. ✅ Fetched the latest documentation to ensure up-to-date installation steps
2. ✅ Identified this as a Next.js 16.2.6 project using the App Router
3. ✅ Installed the `@vercel/speed-insights` package
4. ✅ Used the correct import path (`@vercel/speed-insights/next`) for Next.js 13.5+
5. ✅ Added the component to the root layout file following Next.js best practices
6. ✅ Verified the build completes successfully without errors

### Framework-Specific Considerations

- **Framework**: Next.js 16.2.6 (App Router)
- **Import Path**: Used `@vercel/speed-insights/next` (optimized for Next.js 13.5+)
- **Placement**: Component added at the end of the body element to avoid blocking page rendering
- **Existing Code**: Preserved all existing metadata, styling, and structure

### Verification

- ✅ Build completed successfully (`npm run build`)
- ✅ TypeScript compilation passed with no errors
- ✅ No linting errors (no linter configured in project)
- ✅ No test failures (no tests configured in project)
- ✅ All lock files updated correctly

### Next Steps for User

To enable Speed Insights data collection on Vercel:
1. Deploy this code to Vercel
2. Navigate to the Speed Insights section in your Vercel project dashboard
3. Click the "Enable" button to activate Speed Insights

The component will automatically start collecting and reporting Core Web Vitals and other performance metrics once enabled in the Vercel dashboard.

